## 4. Confidence threshold (functional, not temporal)

**Refined per Qwen P2 review 2026-05-25:** VSF validates by **events**, not by
calendar. Temporal proxies (7/14/30 days) are not the same as functional
proof. Threshold updated to require concrete event evidence.

VSF reaches "internal completeness" when ALL hold:

1. ✓ VSM conformance ≥ 7.5/10 per `VSF_VSM_SCORING.md` (post Qwen refinement, baseline now 5.0)
2. ✓ **≥ 1 S3* → S3 audit cycle completed** with finding emit (not just deploy)
3. ✓ **≥ 1 algedonic trigger fired AND resolved** (real or controlled exercise — observed end-to-end)
4. ✓ **≥ 1 S5 fail-closed event executed and recovered from** (covenant mismatch → abort → operator intervention → restore)
5. ✓ No CRITICAL gap items open (see `GAPS_AND_DEBTS.md`)
6. ✓ Supervisor restart events within expected envelope (no recurrent crashes for the duration of points 2-4)

These are functional gates. rmw3 has final word on judgment calls.

**Note:** This is more stringent than the original temporal criteria.
Beer-faithful: a thing is viable if and only if it demonstrates viability,
not if it has been running for N days without demonstrating anything.

